1
00:02:30,058 --> 00:02:35,058
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,058 --> 00:02:40,058
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,058 --> 00:02:44,058
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,058 --> 00:02:49,058
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,058 --> 00:02:52,058
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,058 --> 00:02:55,058
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,058 --> 00:02:58,058
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:58,058 --> 00:03:01,058
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:01,058 --> 00:03:04,058
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:07,058
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,058 --> 00:03:11,058
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,058 --> 00:03:15,058
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:18,058 --> 00:03:21,058
Luffy escaped the war of the best with his life,

14
00:03:21,058 --> 00:03:24,058
but failed to save his brother from execution.

15
00:03:24,058 --> 00:03:28,058
In the days after, only thoughts of his crew could save him from despair.

16
00:03:29,058 --> 00:03:33,058
It was then that the Dark King Rayleigh made an unexpected suggestion.

17
00:03:33,058 --> 00:03:36,058
Let me offer you some friendly advice.

18
00:03:40,058 --> 00:03:41,058
Back to our captain!

19
00:03:41,058 --> 00:03:45,058
A jailbreak at the Sky Island and the incident on the Winter Island!

20
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:54,058
It's all right.

21
00:03:54,058 --> 00:03:59,058
Luffy?

22
00:04:00,058 --> 00:04:04,058
This is all so unexpected.

23
00:04:04,058 --> 00:04:08,058
Please, Rayleigh, it's far too soon for this. Luffy?

24
00:04:08,058 --> 00:04:11,058
Just my opinion, of course.

25
00:04:11,058 --> 00:04:14,058
But I do think it's what you and your crew need.

26
00:04:15,058 --> 00:04:19,058
Luffy's body and mind alike have suffered from this terrible ordeal.

27
00:04:19,058 --> 00:04:21,058
Although there is truth in your words,

28
00:04:21,058 --> 00:04:24,058
if he cannot heal, then all is meaningless.

29
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,058
But my crew won't know.

30
00:04:29,058 --> 00:04:30,058
That's true.

31
00:04:30,058 --> 00:04:33,058
They'll likely return to Saba Odi as you agreed before.

32
00:04:33,058 --> 00:04:37,058
The events at Marineford were publicized all over the world.

33
00:04:38,058 --> 00:04:40,058
Though you're still reported as missing, I'm sure.

34
00:04:41,058 --> 00:04:42,058
Then I have to go see them.

35
00:04:44,058 --> 00:04:46,058
They're waiting for me.

36
00:04:46,058 --> 00:04:48,058
A promise is a promise, right?

37
00:04:49,058 --> 00:04:51,058
So I need to go to Saba Odi.

38
00:04:51,058 --> 00:05:05,058
Well, then I may have another suggestion for you.

39
00:05:05,058 --> 00:05:06,058
Huh?

40
00:05:11,058 --> 00:05:14,058
Meanwhile, on the floating island of Witheria,

41
00:05:14,058 --> 00:05:20,058
the world's foremost meteorologists are busy coping with a most unruly guest.

42
00:05:20,058 --> 00:05:26,058
Is it truly, truly, truly true?

43
00:05:27,058 --> 00:05:33,058
That young lady tried to escape?

44
00:05:33,058 --> 00:05:35,058
We're a bit high up for that.

45
00:05:35,058 --> 00:05:37,058
I shall explain.

46
00:06:00,058 --> 00:06:03,058
Why where are you off to, young lady?

47
00:06:03,058 --> 00:06:03,618
Young baby.

48
00:06:06,338 --> 00:06:07,418
Carry on.

49
00:06:09,098 --> 00:06:12,098
She danced through the weather field, lickety-split.

50
00:06:12,278 --> 00:06:14,158
Quite irresponsible, I must say.

51
00:06:14,658 --> 00:06:17,638
Then she descended into the balloon terminal and supervised.

52
00:06:19,058 --> 00:06:20,418
Sorry, coming through.

53
00:06:20,718 --> 00:06:22,098
Don't try to stop me.

54
00:06:29,438 --> 00:06:32,058
Then with a heavy backpack at her side,

55
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:34,138
she hijacked the balloon and took off.

56
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:36,058
However...

57
00:06:43,578 --> 00:06:44,058
Whoa!

58
00:06:45,578 --> 00:06:46,118
Ah!

59
00:06:46,478 --> 00:06:47,918
What the heck's going on?

60
00:06:47,998 --> 00:06:49,058
This thing's out of control!

61
00:06:49,818 --> 00:06:50,238
Ah!

62
00:06:54,858 --> 00:06:56,838
It didn't do this last time.

63
00:06:56,918 --> 00:06:58,098
Did I grab a broken one?

64
00:06:59,038 --> 00:06:59,638
Ow!

65
00:07:02,058 --> 00:07:10,478
My balloon's going to crash!

66
00:07:10,698 --> 00:07:11,178
Help!

67
00:07:12,218 --> 00:07:12,598
No!

68
00:07:12,718 --> 00:07:14,158
It's coming straight for us!

69
00:07:14,518 --> 00:07:15,818
Oh, goodness!

70
00:07:16,058 --> 00:07:16,918
We're doomed!

71
00:07:17,258 --> 00:07:17,818
Hurry!

72
00:07:18,018 --> 00:07:18,558
Run away!

73
00:07:18,558 --> 00:07:33,298
And there you have it.

74
00:07:33,518 --> 00:07:35,218
Too much excitement for me.

75
00:07:35,938 --> 00:07:36,258
Hmm.

76
00:07:37,298 --> 00:07:40,918
She may be a fiery young lass, but I didn't think she would do that.

77
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:48,298
Now that I know the what, it's time for us to figure out the why.

78
00:07:48,298 --> 00:07:55,598
I'll give back what I borrowed!

79
00:07:55,798 --> 00:07:57,858
Just let me out of this stupid bubble jail!

80
00:07:58,258 --> 00:07:59,578
I've got somewhere to be, okay?

81
00:07:59,638 --> 00:08:00,458
It's really important!

82
00:08:01,038 --> 00:08:01,838
Come on!

83
00:08:01,938 --> 00:08:02,858
It's just a misunderstanding!

84
00:08:04,138 --> 00:08:05,398
Oh, wait a sec!

85
00:08:05,878 --> 00:08:06,618
Horridus!

86
00:08:06,858 --> 00:08:08,698
Get Horridus and he'll sort this out!

87
00:08:08,938 --> 00:08:09,898
Pretty please!

88
00:08:09,898 --> 00:08:13,638
We're old and you're scary!

89
00:08:13,938 --> 00:08:16,018
Who knows what kind of trap you're plotting!

90
00:08:16,358 --> 00:08:17,698
This is a place of law!

91
00:08:17,938 --> 00:08:19,518
You'll be punished for your crimes!

92
00:08:19,638 --> 00:08:22,378
Yes, what if we shocked her or drowned her a bit?

93
00:08:23,058 --> 00:08:24,878
Which better befits a thief?

94
00:08:26,518 --> 00:08:28,098
Ugh, you guys got it all wrong!

95
00:08:28,578 --> 00:08:30,218
Please, let me out!

96
00:08:30,278 --> 00:08:31,318
At least give me a trial!

97
00:08:31,538 --> 00:08:32,858
No way, Missy!

98
00:08:32,858 --> 00:08:35,978
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

99
00:08:36,118 --> 00:08:36,798
Hey, hey!

100
00:08:36,978 --> 00:08:37,938
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

101
00:08:38,218 --> 00:08:40,198
Oh, hello, Horridus!

102
00:08:40,238 --> 00:08:41,038
Hey, hey, hey!

103
00:08:41,178 --> 00:08:41,958
Hey, hey, hey!

104
00:08:42,298 --> 00:08:42,858
Hey, hey!

105
00:08:44,158 --> 00:08:46,098
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

106
00:08:46,678 --> 00:08:47,678
Well, well!

107
00:08:47,878 --> 00:08:48,838
What a pickle!

108
00:08:49,138 --> 00:08:49,958
Hey, young lady!

109
00:08:50,398 --> 00:08:51,198
Hey yourself!

110
00:08:51,558 --> 00:08:52,758
Another outburst!

111
00:08:52,858 --> 00:08:55,278
You just weren't made to take it easy, were you?

112
00:08:56,158 --> 00:08:57,458
But never fear!

113
00:08:57,878 --> 00:08:59,378
You remember this fellow, right?

114
00:08:59,558 --> 00:09:00,898
Here, I'll show you a trick!

115
00:09:00,898 --> 00:09:03,978
Take your tightly tied wind knots like so!

116
00:09:08,318 --> 00:09:09,358
Horridus, no!

117
00:09:13,138 --> 00:09:15,178
I was counting on you to help me!

118
00:09:15,438 --> 00:09:16,458
Get me out of here!

119
00:09:16,618 --> 00:09:17,778
I'm in a rush, all right?

120
00:09:17,798 --> 00:09:18,598
Are you okay?

121
00:09:19,298 --> 00:09:20,658
Horridus, speak to us!

122
00:09:20,838 --> 00:09:21,898
Tell us you're not dead!

123
00:09:22,498 --> 00:09:25,378
Uh, yes or no?

124
00:09:25,778 --> 00:09:26,638
I mean, maybe.

125
00:09:27,018 --> 00:09:29,758
She hit that kind and gentle man!

126
00:09:29,758 --> 00:09:30,698
What a beast!

127
00:09:30,798 --> 00:09:31,198
Doctor!

128
00:09:31,818 --> 00:09:32,978
Someone call the doctor!

129
00:09:38,518 --> 00:09:39,778
That's most curious.

130
00:09:40,218 --> 00:09:44,918
So she stole an armful of weather balls in our research notes, then tried to make a break

131
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:45,298
for it?

132
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,338
See for yourself.

133
00:09:46,518 --> 00:09:47,558
It's all right here.

134
00:09:49,018 --> 00:09:49,998
Young lady!

135
00:09:49,998 --> 00:09:51,758
I'm a pirate!

136
00:09:51,878 --> 00:09:52,778
What did you expect?

137
00:09:53,098 --> 00:09:54,378
What's wrong with a little theft?

138
00:09:55,898 --> 00:09:57,918
Gotta make a living somehow, don't I?

139
00:09:58,038 --> 00:09:58,758
Simply reprehensible!

140
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:01,118
Such an awful human being!

141
00:10:01,338 --> 00:10:03,058
We have a living in our ditch!

142
00:10:03,218 --> 00:10:04,498
Whatever shall we do!

143
00:10:06,258 --> 00:10:07,498
Just let me go!

144
00:10:08,298 --> 00:10:10,778
You guys don't want me here, and I don't want to be here!

145
00:10:11,138 --> 00:10:12,818
You got back everything I stole!

146
00:10:12,818 --> 00:10:14,118
What does it even matter?

147
00:10:14,658 --> 00:10:17,358
Would you stop flipping out for five seconds and listen to me?

148
00:10:17,438 --> 00:10:18,478
I'm in a hurry here!

149
00:10:18,578 --> 00:10:19,438
This is important!

150
00:10:20,378 --> 00:10:21,638
Don't get too close!

151
00:10:21,998 --> 00:10:23,598
She's terribly violent!

152
00:10:27,198 --> 00:10:28,578
All right, I'm listening.

153
00:10:28,758 --> 00:10:29,258
Let's talk.

154
00:10:29,258 --> 00:10:29,318
Let's talk!

155
00:10:32,758 --> 00:10:37,218
Though I should tell you, stealing a balloon was both foolish and dangerous.

156
00:10:37,218 --> 00:10:39,798
You need proper training to pilot one.

157
00:10:39,998 --> 00:10:41,518
You could have easily died.

158
00:10:43,518 --> 00:10:47,758
Prior to this little outburst, you were perfectly eager to study here with us.

159
00:10:47,978 --> 00:10:49,298
What's gotten into you?

160
00:10:54,098 --> 00:10:54,658
Huh?

161
00:10:56,038 --> 00:10:57,438
Read the front page.

162
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,038
The paper, eh?

163
00:11:01,538 --> 00:11:04,318
You see that article about the pirate named Luffy?

164
00:11:04,738 --> 00:11:06,378
He's the captain of our ship.

165
00:11:06,378 --> 00:11:07,078
Is he?

166
00:11:07,218 --> 00:11:10,918
Oh, I've seen that fellow before.

167
00:11:11,138 --> 00:11:12,498
The boy's a real upstart.

168
00:11:12,778 --> 00:11:15,038
Caused quite the ruckus in Marineford, they say.

169
00:11:15,378 --> 00:11:17,558
He's famous for that straw hat that he wears.

170
00:11:17,938 --> 00:11:19,358
Look at that grin.

171
00:11:19,858 --> 00:11:22,498
He's a charming little rogue, isn't he?

172
00:11:25,458 --> 00:11:28,058
Our crew has been separated for a while now,

173
00:11:28,158 --> 00:11:30,258
so he doesn't even know if we're alive or dead.

174
00:11:30,758 --> 00:11:33,938
I had no idea what he was going through until I read that paper.

175
00:11:33,938 --> 00:11:41,398
I've been taking it easy all this time, while he was down there fighting for his life.

176
00:11:41,398 --> 00:11:50,398
He saw his brother killed right before his eyes.

177
00:11:50,398 --> 00:11:51,018
I didn't even know.

178
00:11:51,018 --> 00:11:52,178
I didn't even know.

179
00:11:52,178 --> 00:11:54,558
I couldn't do anything.

180
00:11:56,258 --> 00:11:57,918
Now he's waiting for me.

181
00:11:57,918 --> 00:12:01,478
And for the rest of the crew, I'm sure.

182
00:12:01,478 --> 00:12:06,438
Luffy is strong, but this is too much to bear.

183
00:12:06,438 --> 00:12:11,598
I want to be there for him.

184
00:12:11,598 --> 00:12:12,998
I want to help him.

185
00:12:18,138 --> 00:12:20,218
Hey, hey, don't cry.

186
00:12:20,438 --> 00:12:21,198
You'll be okay.

187
00:12:21,898 --> 00:12:23,538
Hurry up and let her out.

188
00:12:23,538 --> 00:12:24,878
Oh, we're the real villains.

189
00:12:24,878 --> 00:12:25,898
Look at us.

190
00:12:25,898 --> 00:12:29,118
Abducting an innocent young girl and making her cry.

191
00:12:29,118 --> 00:12:30,338
Give Haradoss the key.

192
00:12:30,378 --> 00:12:31,158
Quickly now.

193
00:12:31,618 --> 00:12:33,238
We're sorry, young lady.

194
00:12:33,458 --> 00:12:34,798
Let's sort this out.

195
00:12:41,538 --> 00:12:42,198
That's hot.

196
00:12:42,298 --> 00:12:43,158
Where did she go?

197
00:12:43,258 --> 00:12:44,618
I don't see Haradoss either.

198
00:12:44,618 --> 00:12:54,238
How did she move so fast?

199
00:12:55,278 --> 00:12:56,618
Thanks for everything.

200
00:12:57,418 --> 00:12:58,278
Bye-bye.

201
00:12:58,498 --> 00:12:58,958
Huh?

202
00:12:59,378 --> 00:13:00,238
Bye-bye?

203
00:13:00,618 --> 00:13:03,418
She pretended to cry to take Haradoss hostage.

204
00:13:03,878 --> 00:13:06,398
And she's stealing our stuff again, too.

205
00:13:06,578 --> 00:13:08,658
We can't let that little harpy escape.

206
00:13:08,898 --> 00:13:10,338
Away we go.

207
00:13:10,338 --> 00:13:14,378
The world below isn't ready for the genius of our research.

208
00:13:14,618 --> 00:13:15,198
I know.

209
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:16,018
I know.

210
00:13:16,298 --> 00:13:17,418
Take me to the sea.

211
00:13:17,718 --> 00:13:18,238
Anywhere.

212
00:13:18,458 --> 00:13:19,838
I can't do it by myself.

213
00:13:20,418 --> 00:13:20,938
Impossible.

214
00:13:21,378 --> 00:13:22,358
Make it possible.

215
00:13:23,898 --> 00:13:25,338
Luffy, hang on.

216
00:13:25,658 --> 00:13:26,798
Just a little bit longer.

217
00:13:27,418 --> 00:13:28,018
I'm sorry.

218
00:13:28,558 --> 00:13:31,198
Every time we've been in trouble, you've been there to help us.

219
00:13:31,638 --> 00:13:32,478
Just this once.

220
00:13:33,038 --> 00:13:34,518
I hope we can return the favor.

221
00:13:34,998 --> 00:13:37,398
Help, thieves, get back here.

222
00:13:39,698 --> 00:13:41,758
You've already captured me, young lady.

223
00:13:42,038 --> 00:13:44,418
You don't need to pretend to cry like that anymore.

224
00:13:44,618 --> 00:13:46,438
Shut up!

225
00:13:46,518 --> 00:13:47,738
Aaaaaaaah!

226
00:13:47,738 --> 00:14:08,738
We now return to Futureland Baltimore,

227
00:14:08,738 --> 00:14:12,738
a mechanical island where the genius Dr. Vegapunk was born.

228
00:14:17,738 --> 00:14:27,738
Grandpa, it's an emergency! The Freak! The Freak! The Freak! I mean the Freak! I mean the Freaky Mr. Freak! I mean, I mean Frankie!

229
00:14:27,738 --> 00:14:30,738
Just calm down and tell me, kitten.

230
00:14:30,738 --> 00:14:37,738
Frankie! He's acting all different, but this time it's scary! He's like some kind of monster!

231
00:14:37,738 --> 00:14:40,738
Someone get me a ship!

232
00:14:40,738 --> 00:14:42,738
He's coming for me!

233
00:14:42,738 --> 00:14:48,738
Tell the truth, kitten. You put something strange in that poor man's stomach to see what would happen, didn't you?

234
00:14:48,738 --> 00:14:51,738
Like habanero juice or kimchi soda or some nonsense.

235
00:14:51,738 --> 00:14:52,738
No! Not this time!

236
00:14:52,738 --> 00:15:11,738
It's an emergency, Gramps. I gotta go see my friends. I know this is sudden, but I won't take no for an answer. I need a ship, dammit! And I need it right now!

237
00:15:11,738 --> 00:15:16,738
A ship? Sorry to say, but that won't be possible.

238
00:15:16,738 --> 00:15:28,738
Huh? We don't have a ship. There's not a single one on the entire island. There's a liner that comes to our country each month to bring us supplies, but we don't have any seafaring vessels of our own.

239
00:15:28,738 --> 00:15:31,738
Alright, fine. When's the liner due back then?

240
00:15:31,738 --> 00:15:34,738
Not for a while yet, I'm afraid. It stopped by last week.

241
00:15:34,738 --> 00:15:38,738
That's no good. I can't wait. There's gotta be some way around this.

242
00:15:38,738 --> 00:15:47,738
You may have noticed this island is surrounded by walls of ice. For better or worse, it works like a fortress.

243
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:53,738
The only ships that can reach us are specially equipped icebreakers and certain navy vessels.

244
00:15:53,738 --> 00:15:59,738
Well, this is bullcrap! I could get supplies to build a ship, but that still wouldn't be fast enough.

245
00:15:59,738 --> 00:16:05,738
Please calm down. Do you want some tea or something?

246
00:16:05,738 --> 00:16:20,738
Hmm. This aroma is just lovely.

247
00:16:20,738 --> 00:16:29,738
Hey! I ain't got time for this! I'm telling you, I gotta blow this joint and I gotta do it fast!

248
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:46,738
My captain needs me right now. I'm lower than dirt if I let him down. Damn it all!

249
00:16:46,738 --> 00:16:49,738
I didn't know.

250
00:16:49,738 --> 00:16:54,738
I understand how important this is to you, but there's nothing you can do but wait.

251
00:16:54,738 --> 00:17:04,738
Oh, here's an idea.

252
00:17:04,738 --> 00:17:05,738
Yeah?

253
00:17:05,738 --> 00:17:11,738
If I recall, Dr. Vegapunk developed an icebreaker. It should still be tucked away in his laboratory, I think.

254
00:17:11,738 --> 00:17:17,738
Of course, it's been years since anyone's touched the thing. Who can say if it still works?

255
00:17:17,738 --> 00:17:21,738
I know it's dangerous, so I'll stay home this time.

256
00:17:21,738 --> 00:17:23,738
Then I know just where to go.

257
00:17:23,738 --> 00:17:27,738
Hold on. You've gone there? Both of you without a word to me?

258
00:17:27,738 --> 00:17:29,738
Yeah! And it was awesome!

259
00:17:29,738 --> 00:17:30,738
What?

260
00:17:32,738 --> 00:17:36,738
If it's broken, then I can fix it. I am a shipwright, after all.

261
00:17:36,738 --> 00:17:38,738
That's not exactly the concern here.

262
00:17:38,738 --> 00:17:40,738
I'm taking this party to the lab!

263
00:17:40,738 --> 00:17:42,738
Wait! Listen to me!

264
00:17:46,738 --> 00:17:48,738
Ugh, it's cold!

265
00:17:58,738 --> 00:18:00,738
We have an intruder!

266
00:18:00,738 --> 00:18:03,738
Someone's broken into Dr. Vegapunk's lab! What should we do?

267
00:18:03,738 --> 00:18:05,738
Dammit!

268
00:18:05,738 --> 00:18:07,738
Apprehend them, but don't use any firearms!

269
00:18:07,738 --> 00:18:11,738
His inventions are too valuable! We can't afford to have even one damaged!

270
00:18:11,738 --> 00:18:12,738
Understand?

271
00:18:12,738 --> 00:18:13,738
Yes, sir!

272
00:18:15,738 --> 00:18:17,738
Get back here!

273
00:18:17,738 --> 00:18:20,738
Crap! It must've tightened security after the last time I broke in!

274
00:18:20,738 --> 00:18:22,738
I can't get anything done with these guys chasing me!

275
00:18:26,738 --> 00:18:28,738
Hold on. I get it now.

276
00:18:29,738 --> 00:18:31,738
We can't shoot in here.

277
00:18:31,738 --> 00:18:35,738
Don't let him get away! Go!

278
00:18:37,738 --> 00:18:39,738
Wait, what do you mean the lab is full of treasure?

279
00:18:40,738 --> 00:18:44,738
Vegapunk is the head of the Navy Science Division, so all of his works are valuable.

280
00:18:45,738 --> 00:18:46,738
Priceless, really.

281
00:18:47,738 --> 00:18:48,738
Our country's very proud of him.

282
00:18:49,738 --> 00:18:52,738
Although, I suppose it's his mind that's the real treasure.

283
00:18:53,738 --> 00:18:57,738
At any rate, he spent his youth working in that lab, tirelessly.

284
00:18:57,738 --> 00:19:03,738
Have you noticed that mountain? A rather unnatural shape, isn't it?

285
00:19:03,738 --> 00:19:07,738
I never gave it much thought. But yeah, there's a story behind it.

286
00:19:07,738 --> 00:19:13,738
It's a project Vegapunk began as a child. It was meant to protect the island's people from frigid weather.

287
00:19:14,738 --> 00:19:19,738
He built it by transforming the animals in the forest into a robotic workforce.

288
00:19:20,738 --> 00:19:25,738
Unfortunately, it remains unfinished. It's a sort of geothermal system to heat up the whole island.

289
00:19:25,738 --> 00:19:37,738
The world just can't keep up with his imagination. That's why so many of his works remain buried here in a state of half completion.

290
00:19:37,738 --> 00:19:50,738
Sometimes, the technology or funds he needed didn't exist. Even though he couldn't get rid of the cold, knowing that he cared, knowing that he worked so hard, warmed our hearts at least.

291
00:19:50,738 --> 00:19:56,738
That story is super depressing.

292
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:58,738
You think so?

293
00:19:59,738 --> 00:20:03,738
But the people here are happy to wait for his return, whenever that may be.

294
00:20:05,738 --> 00:20:12,738
Please respect our feelings and stay out of that lab. After all, it's equipped with a self-destruct button, in case you wanted to know.

295
00:20:12,738 --> 00:20:18,738
But why? Not the button. I mean, why did you think I would want to know that? Like I was gonna press the dumb thing?

296
00:20:19,738 --> 00:20:26,738
Either way, that sounds pretty scary. Why don't we forget about this whole mess and go home? I'll make you some nice hot tea, okay?

297
00:20:27,738 --> 00:20:35,738
Sorry, kiddo. No way. I didn't come all the way out here with no pants on just to turn around. I'm getting that icebreaker if it's the last thing I do.

298
00:20:35,738 --> 00:20:44,738
Don't get me wrong. I appreciate your hospitality, but I read the paper today, and it turns out that my captain has gone through hell and back.

299
00:20:45,738 --> 00:20:48,738
So bye! You guys have a nice life!

300
00:20:49,738 --> 00:20:53,738
I know it's tempting, but no matter what, don't press that self-destruct button!

301
00:20:54,738 --> 00:20:57,738
Would you give it a rest already? Why the hell would I want to do something like that?

302
00:21:06,738 --> 00:21:10,738
Hey! I saw someone down this hallway! Over there! Hurry!

303
00:21:13,738 --> 00:21:15,738
I can't find the ship with them chasing me!

304
00:21:16,738 --> 00:21:17,738
Hulk!

305
00:21:18,738 --> 00:21:21,738
Did you hear? The Marines came by and said someone broke into the lab.

306
00:21:22,738 --> 00:21:24,738
That's not good. Let's just hope they catch him.

307
00:21:25,738 --> 00:21:29,738
They're probably looking to sell stuff on the black market. Even a blueprint from that place would be worth a fortune.

308
00:21:30,738 --> 00:21:31,738
This way?

309
00:21:32,738 --> 00:21:34,738
Well, that was a pain in the butt.

310
00:21:37,738 --> 00:21:45,738
I shouldn't need to remind you, but so much as sneeze on one of Dr. Vegapunk's masterpieces and you'll spend the rest of your life in prison! I don't care if you're a Marine!

311
00:21:46,738 --> 00:21:47,738
Sir!

312
00:21:47,738 --> 00:21:58,738
I can't believe the doctor cooked up all this stuff when he was so young. Cause this is super brilliant work if I've ever seen it.

313
00:21:59,738 --> 00:22:03,738
Half of this is so advanced it'll take another hundred years before the world is ready.

314
00:22:03,738 --> 00:22:08,738
Maybe I don't want to mess with this. As a fellow engineer, I gotta respect the man's work.

315
00:22:12,738 --> 00:22:13,738
Huh?

316
00:22:14,738 --> 00:22:16,738
Sweet! He's got a pirate mark too?

317
00:22:16,738 --> 00:22:17,738
A pirate mark too?

318
00:22:38,738 --> 00:22:43,738
So, hypothetically, if by some crazy chance I press that button like you said...

319
00:22:43,738 --> 00:22:44,738
Mm-hmm.

320
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:45,738
Yeah, go on.

321
00:22:46,738 --> 00:22:48,738
You wouldn't, like, hold it against me, would you?

322
00:22:49,738 --> 00:22:50,738
Of course we would!

323
00:22:51,738 --> 00:22:59,738
News of this incident quickly spread across the world. And history would remember it as Baltimore's nightmare.

324
00:22:59,738 --> 00:23:19,738
Zorro makes a wild dash to the sea as Mihawk watches on. Will the Master Swordsman impart wisdom to Zorro? Or will their reunion end in another deadly duel?

325
00:23:19,738 --> 00:23:23,738
Meanwhile, Luffy begins a daring plan of his own.

326
00:23:24,738 --> 00:23:33,738
On the next One Piece, encounter the Great Swordsman Mihawk! Zorro's self-willed deadly struggle! I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

